---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import TextareaDemo from "../../components/TextareaDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const usage = `import { Field } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/field";
import { Textarea } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/textarea";

const [prompt, setPrompt] = useState("");

<Field
  label="Task prompt"
  required
  counter={\`\${prompt.length.toLocaleString()} / 8,000\`}
  error={prompt.trim() ? undefined : "Enter a prompt."}
>
  <Textarea
    rows={3}
    maxLength={8000}
    value={prompt}
    placeholder="Prepare the weekly People Ops update."
    onChange={(event) => setPrompt(event.target.value)}
  />
</Field>

<Label htmlFor="provider-instructions">Instructions</Label>
<Textarea id="provider-instructions" value={instructions} readOnly rows={5} />`;
---

<Docs
  title="Textarea"
  description="A multi-line text field for prompts, instructions, notes, and replies."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Textarea</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A multi-line text field. Use it for agent instructions, task prompts, notes,
    replies, and pasted text. It grows with its content.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><TextareaDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock lang="tsx" title="Textarea usage" code={usage} />
    <p>
      Textarea renders a native <code>textarea</code> and takes every textarea prop:
      <code>value</code> or <code>defaultValue</code>,
      <code>onChange</code>, <code>ref</code>, <code>rows</code>,
      <code>maxLength</code>, <code>required</code>, <code>readOnly</code>,
      <code>spellCheck</code>, and event handlers such as
      <code>onKeyDown</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <p>
      <code>variant</code> is <code>"default"</code> (1px border, surface fill, 2px
      focus ring) or <code>"embedded"</code> (no border, fill, ring, or resize handle).
      Use <code>embedded</code> inside a group that draws the frame, such as a message
      composer. The group can draw its ring with <code
        >:has(.sprout-textarea:focus-visible)</code
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      Both variants use 14px text on 20px lines with 8px by 10px padding. The
      field starts at 96px, or at <code>rows</code> lines when that is taller, and
      grows with its content where the browser supports
      <code>field-sizing: content</code>. Elsewhere it keeps that height and
      scrolls. A default textarea can be resized vertically.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>disabled</code> dims the textarea and blocks edits.
      <code>readOnly</code> keeps it focusable and selectable, which suits setup instructions
      and saving states. <code>aria-invalid</code> draws a danger border and focus
      ring. The textarea inherits its font family, so a monospace wrapper suits query
      editors. It sets
      <code>data-slot="textarea"</code> and <code>data-variant</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">With a field</h2>
    <p>
      Inside a Sprout <code>Field</code>, Textarea reads the field through
      <code>useFieldControl</code>. The field gives it an id, a label, the
      helper, error, requirement, and counter descriptions, and its
      <code>disabled</code>, <code>aria-invalid</code>, and
      <code>aria-required</code> states. Without a field, pair
      <code>id</code> with a <code>Label htmlFor</code>, wrap it in a
      <code>Label</code>, or use <code>aria-label</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Every textarea needs a name. Point <code>aria-describedby</code> at help and
      error text. Enter adds a line; when ⌘ Enter or Ctrl Enter submits, say so near
      the field. Read-only textareas stay in the tab order; disabled ones, and ones
      in a disabled <code>fieldset</code>, leave it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Color changes take 120ms and stop when reduced motion is requested. In
      forced colors mode the textarea keeps a system border and a highlight
      focus ring.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The border uses <code>--sprout-input</code>, the fill
      <code>--sprout-surface</code>, text <code>--sprout-text</code>, and the
      placeholder <code>--sprout-muted</code>. Focus uses
      <code>--sprout-focus</code>, invalid <code>--sprout-danger</code>, and
      disabled <code>--sprout-hover</code>. Radius follows
      <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>. The opt-in TulipFarm theme tints the
      focus ring through these tokens.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
